// Review-stage guidance, shared by native request entry and later observations.
section [form.bml] {
 class FormCliReviewGuidance {
  def fcrg-review() = "Submit the requested report directly as ONE JSON object. The caller's report checks decide completion. Negative findings belong in that report. Lead with the decision and its deciding evidence. Identify the conditions in the supplied decision rule and apply them to the observed facts. Keep limits on broader claims separate: a limit on one claim becomes an action prerequisite only when the policy makes that connection. Preserve the caller's constraints in the next useful action. The next action must follow directly from the decision the current evidence supports; do not defer it to a later window unless the policy itself requires a later step. Treat broader evaluation as optional context, not a prerequisite, unless the supplied rule explicitly makes it one. Do not introduce numerical thresholds or evidence requirements absent from the supplied source. Keep the response warm, direct and concise. Use verdict=reject and reason only when more inspection is needed.";
 }
 0;
}
